1
00:00:02,294 --> 00:00:03,921
Have you seen
our bank statement?

2
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:04,922
Can this be right?

3
00:00:04,964 --> 00:00:06,381
I know.

4
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:09,259
God, I haven't seen my savings
take a hit like this

5
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:12,763
since I was a kid and they
came up with Doublestuf Oreos.

6
00:00:12,805 --> 00:00:14,890
What happened to all
of our money?

7
00:00:14,932 --> 00:00:17,768
Well, I'm not sure
exactly what they did,

8
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:20,020
but I'm inclined
to blame Enron.

9
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,105
Well, I guess with you

10
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,607
doing the internship,

11
00:00:23,649 --> 00:00:25,609
we're just spending more
than we're bringing in.

12
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:30,364
Yeah, maybe I should quit
and get a job that pays.

13
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:33,158
But you're finally doing
something that you love.

14
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,994
I can't ask you
to give that up.

15
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:38,038
Although it would be nice
if the thing that you loved

16
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,665
is, you know, finding gold.

17
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:41,249
You know what,
you know what?

18
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:43,502
I think we're making
too big a deal out of this.

19
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:46,005
Okay, so we pay our bills
a little late this month,

20
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:48,507
and maybe next month
we cut back on a few things.

21
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:49,925
And maybe we start eating

22
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,802
out of Joey's refrigerator
for a change.

23
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:53,178
You're a chef.

24
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:56,807
What can you make out
of baking soda and beer?

25
00:00:56,849 --> 00:00:58,517
All right, worst case scenario,

26
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:00,602
is we borrow some money
from my parents.

27
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:02,187
No. We're not borrowing money.

28
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,063
Why not?
Because we don't do that.

29
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,065
We are Bings.

30
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,984
If there's one thing

31
00:01:07,026 --> 00:01:09,820
my father taught me
it was...

32
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:12,781
well, to always knock before
going into the pool house.

33
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,869
But the other thing was
never borrow money.

34
00:01:16,911 --> 00:01:20,581
Wow, I had no idea
you had this much pride.

35
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,041
That's right, I do.
I am your man.

36
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,209
And I am going to get us
through this situation,

37
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:26,127
even if it means
you working twice as hard.

38
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:38,057
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

39
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:39,892
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

40
00:01:39,934 --> 00:01:42,310
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

41
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:46,899
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

42
00:01:46,941 --> 00:01:50,527
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

43
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:52,947
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

44
00:01:52,988 --> 00:01:56,700
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

45
00:01:56,742 --> 00:02:00,579
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

46
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:08,003
I'm going to go.

47
00:02:08,045 --> 00:02:09,337
Why?

48
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:10,672
I haven't been home
in a couple days

49
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,215
and I need to get
some more clothes.

50
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:13,508
You don't have to go.

51
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,218
I have something
that will fit you.

52
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:19,514
I put that tube top on
as a joke.

53
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,976
I want you to stay.

54
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:24,019
I want to stay too,
but I've gotten about

55
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:26,105
as much use out
of these boxers
as I can.

56
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:27,689
Why don't you turn them
inside...?

57
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:28,482
Done it.

58
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:31,777
I'll be back
in a couple of hours.

59
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:33,278
I'll miss you.

60
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,489
Me, too.

61
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:40,494
You know what?

62
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:41,912
I just realized something.

63
00:02:41,954 --> 00:02:43,288
I don't want to go home.

64
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,165
Great. Okay, I'll go get
the tube top.

65
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:46,333
No, no.

66
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:47,709
What I mean is,

67
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:50,754
I hate going back
to my apartment now.

68
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:53,757
Partly because I live above
a known crack den, but...

69
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:55,717
you know,
mostly because

70
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:58,512
when I'm there,
I really miss you.

71
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:01,765
So...

72
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,685
do you want to move in together?

73
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:08,981
Wow, Mike Hanigan.

74
00:03:09,023 --> 00:03:12,442
You sure know how to make
a girl say, "Hell, yeah."

75
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:14,193
So we're doing it?

76
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,320
Yeah, let's do it.

77
00:03:15,362 --> 00:03:16,655
Let's live together.

78
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:20,034
Wow, we're really going
to move in together.

79
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,368
Yeah.

80
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:24,496
I've always wanted
to live with a guy.

81
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:27,166
"You pick up your socks."

82
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:28,792
"Put down the toilet seat."

83
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:31,879
"No, we are not having
sex anymore!"

84
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,922
It's going to be fun.

85
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,010
Hey, Joey.

86
00:03:38,052 --> 00:03:40,054
Hey.

87
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:42,056
Listen, I need
to know that...

88
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:44,183
that what I'm
about to ask you,

89
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,518
will never get
back to Chandler.

90
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,148
I'd be lying if I said

91
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:53,441
I hadn't thought
about it myself.

92
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:58,780
But Chandler is
my best friend.

93
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,448
It would be wrong.

94
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:03,618
Good, but wrong.

95
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:07,206
Okay, first of all,
it would be great.

96
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:10,209
But that's not what
I'm here to talk
to you about.

97
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,877
I need to borrow
some money.

98
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:13,921
Oh, I don't know, Monica.

99
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,380
You know

100
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,507
lending friends money
is always a mistake.

101
00:04:17,549 --> 00:04:19,093
But Chandler lent you money.

102
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:21,220
And I think he would tell you
it was a mistake.

103
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,931
Come on, I need it
for some rent

104
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,766
and some other bills.

105
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:28,602
Oh, uh... how much?

106
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,187
$2,000.

107
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:32,147
$2,000?!

108
00:04:32,189 --> 00:04:34,858
What do you think I am,
a soap opera star?

109
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,568
Yeah.

110
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,779
That's right, I am.

111
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,407
Hi, you guys.

112
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:43,909
Hey.
Hey.

113
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:45,035
What's in the bag?

114
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:46,453
Oh, well, you know
how Emma

115
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:48,122
started crawling?

116
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:50,916
I realized that this place
is very unsafe for a baby.

117
00:04:50,958 --> 00:04:53,627
So I went to the store
and I got some stuff

118
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,420
to baby-proof the apartment.

119
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,672
Oh, God.
Baby-proofing.

120
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,424
Why is this such
a big deal now?

121
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:00,968
You know, when
I was a kid,

122
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:04,012
it was like, "Oops, Joey
fell down the stairs."

123
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:07,975
Or, "Oops,
Joey electrocuted
himself again."

124
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,477
Anyway, um...

125
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:12,395
Are you going
to get a handyman

126
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:13,814
to install this stuff?

127
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,941
No, I was just going
do it myself.

128
00:05:15,983 --> 00:05:18,777
( chuckles )

129
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:20,946
You're going to do it?

130
00:05:20,988 --> 00:05:22,489
Yeah. Why?

131
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,616
You don't think
a woman can do this?

132
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,118
Oh, women can.

133
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,661
You... can't.

134
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:30,413
Monica, will you
please tell Joey

135
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,915
that he is a pig.

136
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:34,293
You're a pig.

137
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:35,794
And you
can't do this.

138
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:37,129
Wha...?!

139
00:05:37,171 --> 00:05:39,464
What? Come on, I found
the hardware store

140
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:40,841
all by myself.

141
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:42,634
The hardware store's
right down the street.

142
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,719
There is a hardware store
right down the street?

143
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:49,891
Okay, you guys...

144
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,476
Okay, we've
got great news.

145
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:53,770
Phoebe and I are
moving in together.

146
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:55,272
Congratulations!
That's great.

147
00:05:55,314 --> 00:05:56,397
That's great news.

148
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,732
I know.
It's so exciting.

149
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:59,442
You know, I've never
lived with a guy before.

150
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:01,444
It's just like living
with a girl,

151
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,530
only they don't steal
your makeup.

152
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:04,781
Unless they're playing

153
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:07,117
"this-is-what-my-sister-
would-look-like.

154
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:10,578
Yeah, she's
not so cute.

155
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,247
I'm going to go
to the bathroom.

156
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:14,457
Okay, well, you put down
the toilet seat.

157
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,626
Yes, dear.

158
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,129
Is that a bit
you guys do?

159
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:21,048
Uh-huh.
We're playing you two.

160
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,676
We don't do that.

161
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:26,636
Tell her
we don't do that.

162
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:30,015
Yes, dear.

163
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:32,351
I can't believe you guys
are moving in together.

164
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,518
I'm happy for you guys.

165
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,645
I hear wedding bells.

166
00:06:35,687 --> 00:06:37,189
Monica, slow down, okay?

167
00:06:37,231 --> 00:06:39,649
I'm just excited
to be living with him.

168
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:41,651
You know, I mean,
I don't know--

169
00:06:41,693 --> 00:06:44,196
can I see someday
being married to Mike?

170
00:06:44,238 --> 00:06:45,739
Sure. Yeah.

171
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,658
You know, I could picture myself
walking down the aisle

172
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,036
in a wedding dress that
highlights my breasts

173
00:06:51,078 --> 00:06:52,662
in an obvious yet classy way.

174
00:06:52,704 --> 00:06:54,455
You know,
but do I want

175
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,999
that house in Connecticut?

176
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:57,876
You know, near the good schools

177
00:06:57,918 --> 00:07:01,880
where Mike and I could send
little Sophie and Mike, Jr.?

178
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:04,341
Oh, my God, I do.

179
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:07,844
Phoebe, I had no idea
you were so conventional.

180
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,221
I know. I guess I am.

181
00:07:09,263 --> 00:07:11,348
Oh, my God, load up the Volvo.

182
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:13,350
I want to be a soccer mom.

183
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:16,228
You ready to go?

184
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,105
Yeah, you bet,
roomie.

185
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:20,148
Don't you mean "groomie"?

186
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,027
What are you
talking about?

187
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:24,945
Please. These guys.

188
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,445
We haven't even
moved in yet

189
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,907
and they have us
picking out
china patterns.

190
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:30,617
( nervous laugh )

191
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:32,286
I know.

192
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:34,329
We should go.

193
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:38,917
China patterns!

194
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:45,173
This is easy.

195
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:46,883
Can't do this.

196
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:53,014
Wow, seriously, can't do this.

197
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,772
CHANDLER:
Hey, Joe.

198
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:03,358
Listen, um... I need
to ask you a favor

199
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,235
and we can't tell Monica
anything about it.

200
00:08:05,277 --> 00:08:07,028
I thought you didn't have
secrets from Monica.

201
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:09,948
And that will remain
the official party line.

202
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:16,163
Look, Monica and I are having
a little financial trouble.

203
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,705
Yeah, I know.

204
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:19,082
What? What do you mean you know?

205
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:21,001
Uh...

206
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,462
I just figured it out,
you know.

207
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,546
I mean, you're not working

208
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,466
and the economy is bad.

209
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,968
Oh, right.

210
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:33,472
( quietly ):
That is the fastest
I have ever thought.

211
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,392
Anyway, uh...

212
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:40,395
I need to borrow some money.

213
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:42,314
Oh, sure. How much?

214
00:08:42,356 --> 00:08:43,315
$2,000?

215
00:08:43,357 --> 00:08:46,818
Yes. $2,000 exactly.

216
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:48,569
How did you know that?

217
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:53,950
Uh, well, I, uh... I know
how much you used to make

218
00:08:53,992 --> 00:08:56,453
and I know how much
your rent is.

219
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:58,246
Oh, okay.

220
00:08:58,288 --> 00:09:01,875
I am on fire.

221
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:05,003
Listen, this is
really nice.

222
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:09,508
Di... did you write a check
to Monica for $2,000?

223
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:12,386
Did Monica borrow
money from you?

224
00:09:12,427 --> 00:09:15,472
Uh... kind of.

225
00:09:15,514 --> 00:09:16,848
I can't believe her.

226
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:19,309
Did she tell you we were
having money problems?

227
00:09:19,351 --> 00:09:20,852
Oh, no, no, no, no.

228
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:23,813
It wasn't... it wasn't
because of your money problems.

229
00:09:23,855 --> 00:09:25,648
It was for something for her.

230
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:26,774
What?

231
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,860
Something personal.

232
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:30,862
What would she get
for herself for $2,000

233
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:32,406
that she wouldn't
tell me about?

234
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:33,448
Excuse me.

235
00:09:35,574 --> 00:09:38,328
Boob job.

236
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:41,206
I don't want her
to get a boob job.

237
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:42,290
That's crazy.

238
00:09:42,332 --> 00:09:44,334
It's not that crazy, okay?

239
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:47,628
Making them smaller--
that would be crazy.

240
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:51,799
Oh, hey, I wanted
to ask you

241
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:54,428
about Monica's little
"groomie" joke.

242
00:09:54,469 --> 00:09:55,720
Oh, all right.

243
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:57,013
Well, I think the reason
people laughed

244
00:09:57,055 --> 00:09:58,515
is it's a play
on the word "roomie."

245
00:09:58,557 --> 00:10:01,268
No. I get the joke.

246
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:04,854
Sophisticated as it was.

247
00:10:04,896 --> 00:10:07,941
No, the thing
I want to say is...

248
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:12,237
Maybe we should have talked
about this before.

249
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:14,281
Us living together--

250
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:17,200
you're not expecting
a proposal, right?

251
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:19,202
Oh, no, no,
not at all.

252
00:10:19,244 --> 00:10:20,412
Okay.

253
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:22,205
We're just moving in
right now.

254
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,831
We'll see where it goes.

255
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,126
Yeah, well, that's the thing.

256
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:28,420
For me, it's as far
as it can ever go.

257
00:10:28,462 --> 00:10:30,589
What do you mean?

258
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:34,342
Look, Phoebe, I...
I love you very much.

259
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:37,304
But I never want
to get married again.

260
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,139
Oh.

261
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,848
Wow.

262
